"""Upload an image, or pick one of a few sample photos, and watch a real model
classify it live on CPU - no GPU, no key, nothing to configure.

The model is MobileNetV2, trained on the 1000 ImageNet classes, run with
``onnxruntime``. Weights (about 13 MB) download once from the Hugging Face Hub and
are cached, so a freshly started server pays that cost once, then classifies from
RAM. ``onnxruntime`` and Pillow are this demo's own dependencies, not indah's, and
they're imported lazily inside ``classify`` so the rest of the module works without
either installed.

The sample photos are here because a real classifier is still wrong sometimes -
ImageNet is 1000 narrow categories, and a photo that looks obvious to a person can
land between two of them. The five bundled here (a panda, a zebra, a cat, a guitar,
a lighthouse) are picked because the model gets them right with real confidence, so
the demo shows off what the model does well rather than its edge cases. Upload your
own and you may see it stumble - that's the model being honest, not the demo lying.

Each browser tab gets its own private session, so one person's upload and result
never show up in someone else's tab.

Run it with:  python examples/upload_classify.py
Then open the URL and upload an image, or click a sample. No Node, at install or
at runtime.
"""

import asyncio
import base64

import indah
from indah import (
    Button,
    Card,
    Column,
    Download,
    DownloadFile,
    Image,
    Plot,
    Row,
    Session,
    Signal,
    Spinner,
    Text,
    Upload,
    UploadedFile,
    create_app,
)

